# Request
# The coordinator telling the arbiter that this robot's workload changed, and
# asking for the resulting mission to be gated.
#
# The task is described in the coordinator's flat vocabulary -- the same fields
# TASK_ANNOUNCE carries -- and NOT as mission XML. The coordinator never parses
# a mission: it learns about tasks over the radio, and the agents own the plan.
# So the arbiter applies the edit to the plan it already holds, which also means
# there is no window in which the coordinator is editing a copy the arbiter has
# since replaced.
#
# A service and not a topic because the coordinator needs a verdict it can
# correlate with the request it sent, and /mission/candidate_xml carries no
# request id.

# True when the task is leaving (transferred away, or dropped); false when it
# is arriving (won at auction, or discovered locally).
bool removing

# The task, in the coordinator's terms. Bit indices for required_capabilities
# are amiga_ros2_comms codec.Capability; target_kind is codec.TargetKind:
#   0 NONE   nowhere of its own      1 TREE   target_a is a tree index
#   2 AISLE  target_a is an aisle    3 GPS    target_a/b are lat/lon x 1e7
uint16 task_id
uint16 required_capabilities
uint8 target_kind
int32 target_a
int32 target_b
uint8 priority

# The task's subtree, when this robot has it -- a task shed by our own planner
# carries its XML. Empty when the task was won from a peer, which is the normal
# case: TASK_ANNOUNCE has no room for a subtree, so the arbiter rebuilds one
# from the fields above.
string task_xml

# What the robot that raised this task said about doing it -- the deliberative
# note that preceded the announcement, if one arrived before we bid.
#
# The only field here that no amount of structure could derive. Everything else
# says what the work is; this says something about the world that only the peer
# knows, and it is what the winner's planner is given when it elaborates the
# rebuilt task. Empty is the normal case: most announcements carry no note.
#
# Captured at bid time, not fetched here. A note expires (session.note_ttl_sec)
# well inside the window a note-bearing announcement stays open, so asking for
# it again at GRANT would usually find nothing.
string note

---
# Response

# Whether the edit was committed. False means the coordinator hands the task
# back: release it and re-raise it as an anomaly.
bool accepted

# Whether a formal check actually ran. Distinct from `accepted` on purpose -- a
# plan accepted because no formula could be generated, or because SPIN is not
# installed, has not been verified, and a mission that completes having never
# been checked must not be indistinguishable from one that passed.
bool verified

# Why. On rejection this is the SPIN counterexample, or the name of the
# proposition the plan failed to establish, which is what makes the rejection
# something the next attempt can act on.
string reason
